&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;965&quot; data-end=&quot;1262&quot;&gt;The United States and Israel are preparing for what could become one of the most extensive bombing campaigns of the conflict against Iran's energy infrastructure, according to a CBS News report.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1264&quot; data-end=&quot;1567&quot;&gt;Citing multiple US sources, the broadcaster reported that strikes targeting Iranian energy facilities could begin over the weekend, with discussions also considering whether operations should conclude before global financial markets open on Monday because of concerns over the potential economic impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1569&quot; data-end=&quot;1617&quot;&gt;However, President Donald Trump has not yet given final approval for the operation and no final timeline has been agreed upon, the report said.&lt;/p&gt;
